WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
Next let's walk through how to use the Toolbox control center

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:09.100
When importing multiple projects into Antigravity IDE

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.120
if subfolder names across repositories are identical

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.540
it is difficult to quickly identify which project a folder belongs to

5
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.200
To solve this problem

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.480
I developed this Toolbox extension

7
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.940
integrated directly into the IDE left sidebar

8
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.020
First is the 'Multi-Workspace Management' feature

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.500
It allows us to alias the parent directory name

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.020
into a much more recognizable project title

11
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.720
and quickly switch file explorer scopes

12
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.220
During large project productions

13
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.160
it typically encompasses planning

14
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.940
concept design asset creation to post-processing pipelines

15
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.380
involving a large number of active directories

16
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.180
We can pre-import all workspaces at once

17
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.560
and for projects not currently in progress

18
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.900
use the quick-hide toggle button to collapse them

19
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.920
restoring them whenever needed

20
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.320
while supporting drag-and-drop to reorder projects flexibly

21
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.560
The second core feature is the 'Project Script Launcher

22
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.240
During development

23
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.380
we often have AI write various quick automation scripts

24
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.240
such as .bat batch files or .ps1 PowerShell scripts

25
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.980
However these scripts are scattered across folders

26
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.480
making locating and executing them inconvenient

27
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.420
With this feature

28
00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.120
simply right-click any .bat or .ps1 file in the file explorer

29
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.940
to pin it directly into the Project Script Launcher

30
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.480
Scripts are automatically grouped by workspace

31
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.380
and considering filenames are often in English

32
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.220
the panel supports renaming with custom friendly aliases

33
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.240
You can click buttons to run them in the terminal with 1-click

34
00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.140
or execute with Administrator privileges

35
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.120
significantly boosting operational efficiency

36
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.400
Below that practical utility toolchains are integrated

37
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.360
including 'IDE Preferences' shortcuts

38
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.720
to quickly adjust IDE settings

39
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.380
a toggle for hidden miscellaneous workspace files

40
00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:20.280
and global customization shortcuts to open Antigravity's global config directory

41
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.300
for inspecting and editing core configuration files on the fly

42
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.560
Next is the 'Conversation Brain Snapshot & Disk Cleaner

43
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.040
Whenever we chat with an AI Agent

44
00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.040
the system saves local conversation logs automatically

45
00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.120
which are not cleaned up by default

46
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.160
Over long periods of time

47
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.600
these chat history logs consume substantial disk storage

48
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.100
With this utility we can audit and clean them up safely with ease

49
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.920
Finally at the very top of the panel

50
00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.500
there is a handy 'Open as Editor Tab' button

51
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.020
Sometimes we want to use the Toolbox

52
00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.420
while inspecting the left file explorer in real time

53
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:11.040
simply clicking this button

54
00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.000
converts the sidebar panel directly into an editor workspace tab

55
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.840
keeping the explorer visible on the left

56
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.080
to enable a dual-pane workflow that maximizes productivity
